/**
\page namedcmm_lane iccApplyNamedCmm: named-color and numeric-data lane

\tableofcontents

\section namedcmm_contract Input forms and argv ownership

This tool applies a named-color CMM to legacy, JSON, or IT8 color data.

| Form | Token shape |
|---|---|
| JSON | `iccApplyNamedCmm -cfg config_file` |
| Direct | `iccApplyNamedCmm [-exportcfg file|-exportcfganddata file] [-debugcalc] data encoding interpolation profile intent ...` |

The JSON lane uses the entry array unchanged and accepts exactly three tokens.
The direct lane removes the executable token, then consumes export and
debugging prefixes before `CIccCfgDataApply::fromArgs()` owns the data group.
`CIccCfgProfileSequence::fromArgs()` owns the transform group. Its consumed
count must equal the remaining `argc`; a surplus direct token is a failure,
not a successful partial command.

\dotfile namedcmm-lane.dot "iccApplyNamedCmm data, named-color, and CMM lanes"

\section namedcmm_options Data and transform controls

| Control | Values or form | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| Export | `-exportcfg file`, `-exportcfganddata file` | Export the resolved configuration; the latter also embeds input color data. |
| Debug | `-debugcalc` | Attach calculator-operation log information to output data. |
| Data encoding | `encoding[:precision[:digits]]` | Select final output encoding and formatting. |
| Encoding selector | 0 through 6 | Value, percent, unit float, float, 8-bit, 16-bit, or V2 16-bit. |
| Interpolation | 0 or 1 | Linear or tetrahedral. |
| Sequence modifiers | `-ENV:name value`, `-PCC file` | CMM environment and profile connection conditions for profile pairs. |

The source and destination may be numeric color samples or named colors. If a
named CMM reports `icSigNamedData` at either end, the tool forces the matching
encoding to `icEncodeValue` and follows the name/value conversion path.

\section namedcmm_pcs Input-profile PCS preservation

After `CIccConnectCmm::CreateNamed()` succeeds, the tool decides whether the
first profile is an input profile. When that path exposes a PCS source, it
remaps the signature to a device signature before `ToInternalEncoding()`.
For float, unit-float, and percent inputs it sets `bClip` false, preserving
valid wide PCS values.

\section namedcmm_qa QA example

`iccApplyNamedCmm-quick-check.sh` exercises numeric output, calculator
debugging, profile sequence modifiers, JSON export/replay, and exact argument
rejection using repository fixtures.
*/
